2026-10-13T11:47:40.3261006Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3338950Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3347272Z [0m
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3347561Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3347889Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3348067Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3348594Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3349132Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3349366Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3349588Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3349932Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3350089Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3350503Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3350954Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3351201Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3351392Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3351616Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3351740Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3351877Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3352015Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3352215Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3352288Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3352357Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3352445Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3352638Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3352910Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3357296Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3357446Z I will:
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3357556Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3357736Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3358094Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3358470Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3358812Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3359043Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3359294Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3359723Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3360026Z    /root
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3370270Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3370709Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3379820Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3380365Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3380868Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3381340Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3382028Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3396864Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3397449Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3405176Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3405594Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3405994Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3406162Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3406320Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3406508Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3406732Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3407107Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3407289Z 
2026-10-13T11:47:40.3407389Z If you would like to
